d3d11: stream output of a domain shader

Applies on top of 0013.

With tessellation and no geometry shader, a stream-output "geometry
shader" made from the domain shader's bytecode (CreateGeometryShader-
WithStreamOutput) captured nothing: the tessellation pipeline ignored the
SO layout, SO_STATISTICS / SO_OVERFLOW_PREDICATE queries were refused, and
a draw with no render target, depth buffer or UAV was dropped.  D3D11
wants the output in patch order (then tessellator order), clamped at the
bound buffers in whole primitives, appended after what earlier draws
wrote, and counted in the queries.  The domain shader runs in the mesh
stage, one workload (a strip of a ring) per threadgroup, in any order.

- The tessellation pipeline, when the SO layout is bound, compiles the
  domain shader with SM50_SHADER_TESSELLATION_STREAM (0011's stream: every
  output register of every vertex, the primitives as indices, reserved
  per workload) plus the new SM50_SHADER_TESSELLATION_STREAM_OUTPUT: each
  workload also writes a record (patch, first primitive within its patch,
  first index, primitive count) to SM50_BINDING_INDEX_TESS_STREAM_RECORD
  (dxmt.domain_so_stream_primitives.*, air_tessellation.metal).  A patch's
  workloads are emitted by one object thread in order and sit in the
  payload in that order, so a workload's place in its patch is the count
  of the patch's earlier workloads.
- After the draw the render pass ends and a compute pass runs two
  internal kernels (dxmt_command.metal): so_scan (one threadgroup) sums
  the records per patch, prefix-sums the patches, clamps at every bound
  buffer's capacity from its filled size, advances the filled sizes and
  adds written/needed to the active SO queries; so_write (a thread per
  record) stores every primitive's declared components at
  filled size + (patch offset + primitive in patch) * vertices * stride.
  This is the recorded count -> scan -> write design with the count and
  the capture done by one tessellation pass (the domain shader runs once).
- Each buffer's filled size (BufferFilledSize) is a GPU counter kept with
  the resource; SOSetTargets with an offset sets it, -1 keeps it.
- SO_STATISTICS(_STREAM0..3) and SO_OVERFLOW_PREDICATE(_STREAM0..3):
  a 16-byte shared buffer per bracket, read after the event behind End is
  signaled (stream 0 only; the others read 0).
- RasterizedStream 0 with a domain shader's bytecode: the pipeline the
  draw would have without stream output rasterizes first in the same
  pass, then the stream pass runs.
- A draw with stream-output targets and no attachment gets an
  attachmentless 1x1 pass.
- The graphics pipeline cache key includes the SO layout (a pipeline with
  and one without it, or with two layouts, are different pipelines).
- Instanced tessellation draws with stream output are refused (logged);
  the records do not carry the instance.

Pipelines without an SO layout are unchanged: the new domain-shader
variant field is hashed only when set.

